#Problem APEX 2.7.29
## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Differentiation)
## DBsection(Derivatives of inverse trigonometric functions)
## KEYWORDS('derivative', 'inverse trigonometric')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('2.7')
## Problem1('29')
## Edited July 2023

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");

$a = random(2, 12);
$b = random(2, 5);

$ab = $a * $b;
$bs = $b**2;

$r = 1;
$f = "$a \sin^{-1} $b x";

$x1 = 0;
$y1 = 0;

$deriv = "\frac{$ab}{\sqrt{1-$bs*x^2}}";
$m     = $ab;
$ans   = Compute("$ab x");

BEGIN_PGML

Find the equation of the line tangent to the graph
of [`f`] at the indicated [`x `] value.
[```
  y = [$f], \quad x = [$x1]
```]

Tangent line: [`y = `] [_]{$ans}{20}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

Find the derivative: 
[```
  \dfrac{d}{dx}\left[ [$f] \right] = [$deriv],
```]
and plug in [`x = [$x1]`] to get [` m = [$m] `].  Then the tangent line is
[```
y = [$a*$b] x.
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();

